# [[ .Name ]]
[[ if eq .Kind "qmock" ]]
A qmock: a stand-in quanar for developing quans. It loads quans exactly like a
quanar, but its core answers the qua with stand-in behaviour.
[[ else ]]
The quanar: it gives quans a place to live. It holds no business logic.
[[ end ]]
[[- if not .Quas ]]
> **No qua yet.** A [[ .Kind ]] plugs a qua's core in for its quans; without one
> they cannot reach it. Add a qua to `package.json`, implement its `QuanarCore`
> in `src/core/qua-core` and replace the local `QuanManifest` in `src/types`.
[[ end ]]

- `src/main.tsx` shares React and the qua on `window`, plugs the core into the qua, and starts.
- `src/core/qua-core` implements the qua: this is where `increment` really happens.
- `src/core/quan-loader` loads a built quan with a script tag and reads its manifest.
- `src/config` lists the quans to load and where each one is served from.
- `src/router` and `src/layouts` mount every quan's routes inside the header and sidebar.
- Lines marked `// qu:` are where `qu` plugs in a qua when a new quan brings one.

```sh
npm run dev      # http://localhost:[[ .Port ]]
```

Start the quans first (`npm run watch` in each quan).
